description:
Owner ruling C (~/.claude/jobs/0028abca/tmp/reports/coordinator-owner-rulings-2026-11-06-evening.md), which replaces the on-box-alarm plan of the coordinator watchdog brief. The box PUBLISHES and AWS ALARMS (IB-150). DO: watchdog.py → metric publisher (systemd timer, 1–5 min, Python 3.9), with PutMetricData to the namespace IB-150 defines.
Metrics:
- MemAvailable, swap, container RSS (bot, postgres), restarts, healthz;
- per liq venue: heartbeat age and prints/min;
- the OI loop: last evaluated close (age);
- Binance weight/min;
- the publisher heartbeat itself.
No venue calls: 0 weight. Logs: the docker awslogs driver or the CloudWatch agent for the bot, postgres and caddy, with retention set in IB-150; before shipping, prove no token, ib_session= or secret reaches the logs (the existing token-shape grep over a day of logs). Tests: publisher readings per metric with stubbed sources, the --dry-run printout, and a failure to publish never breaking the box. Live: after IB-150 grants the IAM, the metrics are visible in CloudWatch. Review → merge → sync-box → enable.

Owner ruling B (~/.claude/jobs/0028abca/tmp/reports/coordinator-owner-rulings-2026-11-06-evening.md). Verified in code by the coordinator:
- level-alert-loop.ts:210 levelEventOn continue (WO has not been journalled since 13:06);
- perCoin[sym].enabled false at funding :220, levels :347, liq :155;
- the levels daily filter :293 (PDH/PDL never computed).
Type-wide enabled and OI sendHidden are already correct. DO: evaluate and journal every kind/event/coin in alert_symbols; every switch decides only sending; the row says why it was not sent (muted + which switch). Admin help text: «выключено = не присылать; в журнал пишется всегда» (ru/en). Backfill WO (and PDH/PDL if cheap) from 2026-11-06T13:06:05Z as source=backfill, through the history gate. State the extra DB rows per week. Specs: per switch, a muted event is journalled, not sent; a composition spec over the shipped loops; first-live-level stays correct (its bands read sends). Review → merge → deploy → watch CLEAN.

Seen by dev-1 in IB-150's log measurement (~/.claude/jobs/0028abca/tmp/reports/dev-1-IB-150.md «Error-rate baseline»). DO, read-only first:
- per hour since 13:57, the count of bybit silences versus bybit prints in the tape, and the same for binance and okx;
- whether a reconnect restores prints;
- whether a /public control topic on the same socket stays live (the fstream lesson).
Name the mechanism: genuinely quiet market, a route or topic change, or a reconnect gap. Only then decide on a fix. Per AGENTS.md, a number becomes a rule only after repetition. A liq heartbeat that says alive while prints stop is exactly what IB-149's metrics must not miss; tell dev-3 what the recorder can or cannot see.
ADDED (dev-3, IB-149): the bybit/okx socket arms its silence-reconnect only after a FIRST message (lastMessageAt === null → no reconnect). A socket that opens on a dead route never reconnects, and nothing records it. collector_heartbeats is a process timer, not the stream. ops/watchdog.ts logs a warn per stream silent for > 3 min (the age of the last liquidation); these are the rising lines. Include the never-first-message case in the fix, with a spec that opens a mute socket and expects a reconnect.

Owner ruling via the coordinator (~/.claude/jobs/0028abca/tmp/reports/coordinator-instrument-liq-profile-2026-11-06.md); mockups coordinator-instr-liq-mockup-{desktop,phone}.png, section Б only (variant А is NOT wanted). DO:
- remove the table (desktop and phone), keeping a link «все ликвидации <COIN> списком →» to /liquidations filtered by the coin;
- the profile: desktop attached right of the price pane on the SAME price scale, following vertical zoom/scroll and the visible time range; phone a horizontal histogram under the chart, high price on top; longs left #ef5350, shorts right #26a69a; a current-price mark; level lines if cheap;
- data: ALL liquidations of the coin in the visible range, three venues; ~20–40 adaptive bands;
- tooltip/tap: price range, longs $ / shorts $, count, venue split;
- the undercount note stays; a missing venue shows as missing, never $0 (IB-BUG-011);
- one line of help (ru/en); times via IB-152's formatter.
The aggregation is a pure function with a spec, including band edges and a spec that FAILS if computed from a top-N subset. A new endpoint states its DB rows per request and its cache; weight 0. Extract, don't grow instrument.component.ts (250). Acceptance: side-by-side PNGs at 1240/390 against the mockup, innerWidth == 390, npm test + the whole dashboard e2e under lockf. Review → merge → deploy → CLEAN; before/after PNGs to the coordinator for the owner.
